   "source": [
    "## Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) is one of the leading chronic diseases worldwide and continues to place a significant burden on healthcare systems. Early identification of individuals at risk allows healthcare providers to recommend preventive interventions before complications develop.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project develops an end-to-end machine learning workflow for predicting Type 2 diabetes risk using responses from the CDC Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS) 2023 survey.\n",
    "\n",
    "The project not only compares several machine learning algorithms but also explains model predictions using Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) techniques including SHAP and LIME, making predictions transparent and suitable for healthcare decision support."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6b82608",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Business Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "Healthcare providers often rely on laboratory tests to diagnose diabetes. However, many risk factors associated with Type 2 diabetes are already available through routine health questionnaires.\n",
    "\n",
    "An interpretable machine learning model capable of estimating diabetes risk from survey responses could:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Support early screening\n",
    "- Identify high-risk individuals\n",
    "- Prioritize preventive healthcare\n",
    "- Improve public health interventions\n",
    "- Increase model transparency using Explainable AI"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "29b1f84e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Problem Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "Despite advances in healthcare, many individuals with Type 2 Diabetes remain undiagnosed until complications have already developed. Traditional screening approaches often rely on laboratory testing and clinical assessments, which may not be readily accessible for large-scale population screening.\n",
    "\n",
    "Given the availability of comprehensive health survey data, there is an opportunity to develop an accurate and interpretable machine learning model capable of identifying individuals at elevated risk of Type 2 Diabetes. Such a model can assist healthcare professionals in prioritizing high-risk individuals for further screening, supporting early intervention strategies, and informing evidence-based public health policies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0956a70b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Project Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "To develop an interpretable machine learning system capable of predicting the risk of Type 2 Diabetes using BRFSS 2023 survey data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Specific Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "- Clean and preprocess BRFSS 2023 survey data for machine learning.\n",
    "- Perform exploratory data analysis to understand demographic, behavioral, and clinical factors associated with diabetes.\n",
    "- Engineer relevant features for improved predictive performance.\n",
    "- Train and compare Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, and XGBoost classifiers.\n",
    "- Evaluate model performance using appropriate classification metrics.\n",
    "- Explain model predictions using SHAP and LIME.\n",
    "- Develop an interactive Streamlit dashboard for diabetes risk prediction and visualization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "576c0cf0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stakeholders\n",
    "\n",
    "### Primary Stakeholders\n",
    "\n",
    "- Healthcare providers and clinicians\n",
    "- Individuals at risk of Type 2 Diabetes\n",
    "- Public health agencies\n",
    "- Community health programs\n",
    "\n",
    "### Secondary Stakeholders\n",
    "\n",
    "- Medical researchers\n",
    "- Academic institutions\n",
    "- Health insurance organizations\n",
    "- Government policymakers\n",
    "- Non-governmental health organizations (NGOs)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e582b6b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Model Performance Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The success of the predictive models will be evaluated using:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Accuracy (Target: ≥80%)\n",
    "- Precision\n",
    "- Recall\n",
    "- F1-score\n",
    "- ROC-AUC Score\n",
    "- Confusion Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "Special emphasis will be placed on Recall, as correctly identifying individuals at risk of diabetes is more important than minimizing false positives.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Success Criteria\n",
    "\n",
    "The project will be considered successful if:\n",
    "\n",
    "- At least one model achieves strong predictive performance.\n",
    "- SHAP successfully explains global feature importance.\n",
    "- LIME provides local explanations for individual predictions.\n",
    "- The Streamlit dashboard allows users to:\n",
    "  - Predict diabetes risk for an individual.\n",
    "  - Upload datasets for batch predictions.\n",
    "  - Visualize prediction probabilities.\n",
    "  - Download prediction reports."
   ]
  },
