    "## 2.5 Variable Categories\n",
    "\n",
    "The BRFSS questionnaire covers a broad range of health-related information. The variables can be grouped into several categories relevant to diabetes prediction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b66bf15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "| Category | Examples |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **Demographics** | Age, Sex, Education, Income, Marital Status |\n",
    "| **Lifestyle** | Smoking, Alcohol Consumption, Physical Activity |\n",
    "| **Clinical Conditions** | High Blood Pressure, Cholesterol, BMI |\n",
    "| **Medical History** | Heart Disease, Stroke, Kidney Disease |\n",
    "| **Preventive Care** | Routine Checkups, Vaccinations |\n",
    "| **Social Determinants** | Employment, Housing, Healthcare Access |\n",
    "| **Derived CDC Variables** | BMI Categories, Physical Activity Index, Race Groups |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e99fe4a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.6 Target Variable\n",
    "\n",
    "The target variable for this study is **DIABETE4**, which records respondents' diabetes status.\n",
    "\n",
    "The original variable contains multiple response categories, including diabetes diagnosis, prediabetes, gestational diabetes, and unknown responses.\n",
    "\n",
    "For supervised machine learning, the target will later be transformed into a binary classification problem:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **1** → Diagnosed with Type 2 Diabetes\n",
    "- **0** → No Diabetes\n",
    "\n",
    "Responses that cannot reliably represent either class will be removed during data preprocessing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f359d3bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.7 Data Quality Considerations\n",
    "\n",
    "As with many large-scale health surveys, the BRFSS dataset requires substantial preprocessing before modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key considerations include:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Missing values represented by coded responses such as *Refused* and *Don't Know*.\n",
    "- Survey-specific numerical coding rather than descriptive labels.\n",
    "- Variables applicable only to specific respondent groups.\n",
    "- Potential class imbalance between diabetic and non-diabetic respondents.\n",
    "- High dimensionality, with many variables unrelated to diabetes prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "These issues will be addressed systematically during the Data Preparation stage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4bb8359f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.8 Feature Selection Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "Although the original dataset contains **350 variables**, only a subset is relevant for predicting Type 2 Diabetes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Feature selection will be guided by:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Medical literature on diabetes risk factors\n",
    "- CDC BRFSS documentation\n",
    "- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "- Statistical relevance\n",
    "- Feature importance from machine learning models\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to retain clinically meaningful variables while reducing redundancy, improving model performance, and enhancing interpretability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab1a2ecc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.9 Section Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The exploration of the BRFSS 2023 dataset establishes a strong foundation for developing an interpretable machine learning model for Type 2 diabetes risk prediction. With **433,323 adult respondents** and **350 variables**, the dataset captures a comprehensive range of demographic, behavioral, clinical, and socioeconomic factors known to influence diabetes risk. Its breadth and diversity provide a valuable basis for investigating the complex interactions underlying Type 2 Diabetes.\n",
    "\n",
    "As with many large-scale epidemiological surveys, the dataset contains coded responses, survey-specific administrative variables, and missing values that require careful preprocessing before meaningful analysis can be performed. Addressing these challenges is an essential step toward ensuring data quality, improving model reliability, and enhancing the interpretability of subsequent analyses.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the initial assessment confirms that the BRFSS 2023 dataset is well suited to the objectives of this study. The next phase focuses on **Data Preparation**, where relevant variables will be selected, missing and invalid responses handled, survey codes recoded into meaningful representations, and the target variable transformed into a binary classification problem. These preprocessing steps will produce a clean and structured analytical dataset suitable for exploratory data analysis, predictive modeling, and explainable artificial intelligence (XAI)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a74038b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "---\n",
    "# 3. Data Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "The BRFSS 2023 dataset is a large-scale public health survey designed for epidemiological surveillance rather than machine learning. Consequently, the raw data contains survey administration variables, encoded categorical responses, and standardized missing-value codes that require preprocessing before analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective of this phase is to transform the raw survey data into a clean, consistent, and analysis-ready dataset while preserving the integrity of the original information. Proper data preparation improves data quality, enhances model reliability, and ensures that subsequent exploratory analysis and predictive modeling are based on meaningful and valid observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following preprocessing tasks are performed in this section:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Select the variables required for Type 2 diabetes prediction.\n",
    "- Decode SAS XPORT byte-string values where necessary.\n",
    "- Handle BRFSS-specific missing and invalid response codes.\n",
    "- Construct the binary diabetes target variable.\n",
    "- Verify data quality through data type and missing-value assessment.\n",
    "- Produce and save the cleaned analytical dataset for \n",
    "  exploratory analysis and model development.\n",
    "- Assess target variable distribution and document \n",
    "  class balance for downstream modelling decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The resulting dataset provides a reliable foundation for the exploratory analysis presented in the next section and the machine learning models developed later in this project."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ca2c0bb7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.1 Variable Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "The BRFSS 2023 dataset contains **350 variables**, many of which relate to survey administration, data collection procedures, weighting, geographic identifiers, or health conditions outside the scope of this study. While these variables are valuable for broader public health surveillance, they are not all relevant to predicting Type 2 Diabetes.\n",
    "\n",
    "To improve computational efficiency, reduce model complexity, and enhance interpretability, only variables with established clinical or epidemiological relevance to Type 2 Diabetes were retained. The selection was informed by existing medical literature, recommendations from organizations such as the American Diabetes Association (ADA), and previous diabetes prediction studies using BRFSS data.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Variable | Label | Domain | Clinical Justification |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `_BMI5` | BMI | Anthropometric | Strongest modifiable predictor of T2DM |\n",
    "| `_AGE80` | Age | Demographic | Risk increases significantly after 45 |\n",
    "| `SEXVAR` | Sex | Demographic | Differential risk between males and females |\n",
    "| `_IMPRACE` | Race/Ethnicity | Demographic | Higher prevalence in certain ethnic groups |\n",
    "| `GENHLTH` | General Health | Health Status | Poor self-rated health associated with chronic disease |\n",
    "| `PHYSHLTH` | Physical Health Days | Health Status | Proxy for underlying illness burden |\n",
    "| `SMOKE100` | Smoking | Lifestyle | 30–40% elevated T2DM risk in smokers |\n",
    "| `_TOTINDA` | Physical Activity | Lifestyle | Inactivity is a major modifiable risk factor |\n",
    "| `EDUCA` | Education Level | Socioeconomic | Influences health literacy and behaviour |\n",
    "| `INCOME3` | Income Level | Socioeconomic | Affects healthcare access and healthy living |\n",
    "| `_RFHYPE6` | Hypertension | Clinical | Shares metabolic pathways with T2DM |\n",
    "| `_RFCHOL3` | High Cholesterol | Clinical | Linked to insulin resistance |\n",
    "| `CHCKDNY2` | Kidney Disease | Clinical | Strongly associated with diabetes |\n",
    "| `_MICHD` | Heart Disease | Clinical | Shares major risk factors with T2DM |\n",
    "\n",
    "The target variable, **`DIABETE4`**, was retained separately and later transformed into a binary outcome indicating whether a respondent has Type 2 diabetes.\n",
    "\n",
    "This targeted selection reduces the dimensionality of the dataset while preserving the variables most relevant for developing an accurate and interpretable diabetes risk prediction model."
   ]
  },
