    "**Observation** \n",
    "\n",
    "Inspecting the raw unique values per feature confirms the presence of BRFSS\n",
    "survey-specific special codes across multiple variables and establishes the\n",
    "exact recoding rules required in the next step.\n",
    "\n",
    "`_BMI5` contains thousands of distinct continuous values ranging from\n",
    "approximately 1,202 to 9,984, confirming that the variable is stored as BMI\n",
    "multiplied by 100 and requires rescaling. No special survey codes are present\n",
    "the missing values in this variable are structural NaNs rather than coded\n",
    "responses.\n",
    "\n",
    "`_AGE80`, `SEXVAR`, `_IMPRACE`, and `_MICHD` contain only their expected valid\n",
    "response codes with no special values present, requiring no recoding.\n",
    "\n",
    "`GENHLTH` contains values `7` and `9` alongside valid responses `1`–`5`,\n",
    "representing *Don't Know* and *Refused* respectively. `PHYSHLTH` contains the\n",
    "full range of valid day counts `1`–`30`, the special code `88` representing\n",
    "*None / zero bad days* which must be recoded to `0` rather than `NaN`, and\n",
    "codes `77` and `99` representing *Don't Know* and *Refused* which are true\n",
    "missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "`SMOKE100`, `_TOTINDA`, `EDUCA`, `_RFHYPE6`, `_RFCHOL3`, and `CHCKDNY2`\n",
    "each contain `9` as a *Don't Know / Refused* code alongside their valid\n",
    "response categories. `INCOME3` contains codes `77` and `99` in addition to\n",
    "valid ordinal values `1`–`11`.\n",
    "\n",
    "`DIABETE4` contains all six response categories codes `1`–`4` representing\n",
    "meaningful diabetes status, and codes `7` and `9` representing non-informative\n",
    "responses which will be handled during target variable construction in\n",
    "Section 3.5.\n",
    "\n",
    "These findings confirm the recoding strategy applied in Section 3.4 and\n",
    "establish that no unexpected or undocumented codes are present in the selected\n",
    "variables."
   ]
