   "source": [
    "## 3.4 BRFSS Special Code Recoding\n",
    "\n",
    "The BRFSS survey uses standardised numeric codes to represent non-informative\n",
    "responses such as *Don't Know*, *Not Sure*, *Refused*, and *Not Applicable*.\n",
    "These codes are not true numeric values and must not be treated as such by\n",
    "machine learning algorithms. If left in place, they would introduce significant\n",
    "bias for example, a PHYSHLTH value of 77 would be interpreted as 77 poor\n",
    "health days rather than a missing response.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following recoding rules are applied based on the BRFSS 2023 codebook and\n",
    "confirmed by inspecting the unique values present in each selected variable:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Variable | Special Codes → Action |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `GENHLTH` | 7, 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `PHYSHLTH` | 88 → `0` (no bad days) · 77, 99 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `SMOKE100` | 7, 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `_TOTINDA` | 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `EDUCA` | 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `INCOME3` | 77, 99 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `_RFHYPE6` | 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `_RFCHOL3` | 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `CHCKDNY2` | 7, 9 → `NaN` |\n",
    "| `_BMI5` | Divide by 100 (stored as integer × 100 in BRFSS) |\n",
    "\n",
    "Variables `_AGE80`, `SEXVAR`, `_IMPRACE`, and `_MICHD` contained no special\n",
    "codes and required no recoding. The target variable `DIABETE4` is handled\n",
    "separately in Section 3.5."
   ]
  },
