   "source": [
    "### 4.3.2 Correlation Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "A correlation matrix is computed across all 14 features and the binary target\n",
    "variable to identify linear relationships between variables. High correlation\n",
    "between predictor variables may indicate multicollinearity, which can affect\n",
    "model stability. Correlations between predictors and the target variable\n",
    "provide an initial indication of predictive value.\n",
    "\n",
    "Pearson correlation is used for continuous variables, with the understanding\n",
    "that ordinal BRFSS variables are treated as approximately continuous for the\n",
    "purposes of this exploratory analysis."
   ]
  },
