    "**Observations**\n",
    "\n",
    "The heatmap shows that several features exhibit stronger linear associations with diabetes than others. Variables such as age, general health, BMI, and high blood pressure demonstrate relatively higher positive correlations with the target variable, whereas features such as income and education show weaker negative correlations. Although most correlation coefficients are modest, this is expected in healthcare datasets where disease outcomes are influenced by multiple interacting factors rather than a single predictor.\n",
    "\n",
    "These results complement the earlier bivariate analysis by quantitatively ranking the strength of each feature's association with diabetes and provide additional evidence for feature importance prior to model development."
