   "source": [
    "## 4.4 Exploratory Data Analysis Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The exploratory data analysis provided a comprehensive understanding of the dataset prior to predictive modelling. Univariate analysis described the distribution and characteristics of the target variable and predictor variables, while bivariate analysis identified meaningful relationships between individual features and diabetes prevalence. Variables such as age, BMI, general health, high blood pressure, and physical health exhibited stronger associations with diabetes, whereas factors such as income and education showed comparatively weaker relationships.\n",
    "\n",
    "Multivariate analysis further assessed the overall structure of the dataset through missing value analysis and correlation analysis. The missing value assessment confirmed that the dataset was largely complete, with only a small number of variables containing missing values. The correlation matrix indicated no evidence of severe multicollinearity among the predictor variables, while the feature-to-target correlation analysis highlighted the variables most strongly associated with diabetes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the exploratory analysis confirmed that the dataset was suitable for machine learning, identified the most informative predictors, and provided a strong foundation for the model development and evaluation presented in the following chapter."
   ]
