    "---\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 6. Model Development\n",
    "\n",
    "This section develops and evaluates multiple machine learning classification\n",
    "algorithms to identify the best-performing model for Type 2 diabetes risk\n",
    "prediction. Models are trained on the SMOTE-resampled training set produced\n",
    "in Section 5 and evaluated on the held-out test set using a consistent and\n",
    "clinically motivated set of performance metrics.\n",
    "\n",
    "The modelling workflow is organised into the following stages:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 1 — Baseline Model**\n",
    "Logistic Regression is trained first to establish an interpretable performance\n",
    "benchmark. All subsequent models must exceed this baseline on Recall and\n",
    "ROC-AUC to justify their additional complexity.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 2 — Tree-Based Classifiers**\n",
    "A Decision Tree and a Random Forest are trained as non-linear alternatives\n",
    "to the baseline, introducing ensemble learning and evaluating whether\n",
    "bagging improves performance over a single tree.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 3 — Gradient Boosting Classifiers**\n",
    "XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost are trained as sequential ensemble methods,\n",
    "representing the state-of-the-art approaches for structured tabular data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 4 — Initial Model Comparison**\n",
    "All six models are compared across Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-Score,\n",
    "and ROC-AUC to identify performance patterns and configuration issues.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 5 — Hyperparameter Tuning**\n",
    "Gradient boosting models are retrained with corrected configurations and\n",
    "decision threshold optimisation is applied to maximise Recall on the\n",
    "positive class.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 6 — Final Model Selection**\n",
    "The best-performing model after tuning is selected, evaluated in full, and\n",
    "prepared for the Explainability analysis in Section 7.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "All models are trained on `X_train_res` and `y_train_res`  the scaled,\n",
    "SMOTE-resampled training set and evaluated on `X_test_scaled` and `y_test` the scaled test set retaining the original 6.2:1 class distribution.\n",
    "This ensures that evaluation metrics reflect real-world conditions rather\n",
    "than the artificially balanced training environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "144b0c9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6.1 Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "Given the clinical context of this study, model performance is assessed using\n",
    "the following metrics:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Formula | Clinical Relevance |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Accuracy** | (TP + TN) / Total | Overall correctness misleading with imbalance |\n",
    "| **Precision** | TP / (TP + FP) | Of predicted diabetics, how many truly are |\n",
    "| **Recall** | TP / (TP + FN) | Of true diabetics, how many were identified |\n",
    "| **F1-Score** | 2 × (P × R) / (P + R) | Balance of Precision and Recall |\n",
    "| **ROC-AUC** | Area under ROC curve | Overall discrimination ability |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recall is the primary metric.** A false negative a diabetic patient\n",
    "classified as healthy carries greater clinical harm than a false positive.\n",
    "Accuracy alone is not used as a success criterion, as a naive majority-class\n",
    "classifier would already achieve 86% without any learning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c5d1ed8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6.2 Helper Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "To ensure consistency across all machine learning experiments, reusable helper functions were implemented for model training, evaluation, ROC curve generation, confusion matrix visualization, and performance reporting. These functions eliminate duplicated code while ensuring that every classifier is evaluated under identical conditions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 53,
   "id": "ffd66139",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "✅ Helper functions defined\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
    "    f1_score, roc_auc_score, confusion_matrix,\n",
    "    ConfusionMatrixDisplay, RocCurveDisplay,\n",
    "    classification_report,\n",
    ")\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Store results for comparison\n",
    "results = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate_model(name, model, X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Train, evaluate and store results for a single model.\n",
    "    Returns a dictionary of performance metrics.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Train\n",
    "    start = time.time()\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "    train_time = round(time.time() - start, 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Predict\n",
    "    y_pred      = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "    y_pred_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Metrics\n",
    "    metrics = {\n",
    "        \"Accuracy\":  round(accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)       * 100, 2),\n",
    "        \"Precision\": round(precision_score(y_test, y_pred)      * 100, 2),\n",
    "        \"Recall\":    round(recall_score(y_test, y_pred)         * 100, 2),\n",
    "        \"F1-Score\":  round(f1_score(y_test, y_pred)             * 100, 2),\n",
    "        \"ROC-AUC\":   round(roc_auc_score(y_test, y_pred_prob)   * 100, 2),\n",
    "        \"Train Time (s)\": train_time,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    results[name] = metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Print summary\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{'='*50}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  {name}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{'='*50}\")\n",
    "    for k, v in metrics.items():\n",
    "        unit = \"%\" if k != \"Train Time (s)\" else \"s\"\n",
    "        print(f\"  {k:<20} {v}{unit}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    return model, y_pred, y_pred_prob\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def plot_confusion_matrix(name, y_test, y_pred, ax):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Plot a styled confusion matrix on a given axis.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "    disp = ConfusionMatrixDisplay(\n",
    "        confusion_matrix=cm,\n",
    "        display_labels=[\"No Diabetes\", \"Diabetes\"]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    disp.plot(ax=ax, colorbar=False, cmap=\"Blues\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(name, fontsize=11, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Predicted\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Actual\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Helper functions defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80705b80",
