    "**Observation — Model Comparison Summary**\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial model comparison reveals an unexpected performance pattern across the six\n",
    "classifiers. Contrary to the hypothesis that gradient boosting ensemble methods\n",
    "would outperform the linear baseline, **Logistic Regression achieves the highest\n",
    "Recall of 75.88%**  the primary evaluation metric making it the strongest\n",
    "performing model in its current configuration.\n",
    "\n",
    "The performance split across models falls into two distinct groups:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Group 1 — High Recall, Lower Accuracy**\n",
    "Logistic Regression and Decision Tree prioritise positive class detection,\n",
    "achieving Recall values of 75.88% and 66.28% respectively at the cost of\n",
    "lower overall Accuracy. These models are more aligned with the clinical\n",
    "objective of this study.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Group 2 — High Accuracy, Low Recall**\n",
    "Random Forest, XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost all achieve Accuracy above\n",
    "77% but Recall below 66%, with the three gradient boosting models recording\n",
    "critically low Recall values between 17% and 25%. This pattern is attributable\n",
    "to double class-balancing SMOTE was applied to the training set and class\n",
    "weight parameters were simultaneously set within each model, causing the\n",
    "decision boundary to shift toward the majority class.\n",
    "\n",
    "The **ROC-AUC scores are remarkably consistent** across all six models\n",
    "ranging narrowly from 79.50% (Decision Tree) to 82.00% (CatBoost)\n",
    "indicating that all models have comparable overall discriminatory power.\n",
    "The key differentiator is not the ability to rank patients by risk, but\n",
    "the operating point at which the decision threshold is set.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key takeaways for next steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Logistic Regression is the current leading candidate with Recall 75.88%\n",
    "  and ROC-AUC 81.33%.\n",
    "- Gradient boosting models must be retrained without class weight parameters\n",
    "  to isolate the effect of SMOTE alone.\n",
    "- Threshold tuning on the best ROC-AUC model (CatBoost 82.00%) may\n",
    "  produce higher Recall than retraining.\n",
    "- The Decision Tree underperforms on both Recall and ROC-AUC and is\n",
    "  eliminated from further consideration."
   ]
