   "source": [
    "### 6.6.2 Initial Training Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial training round evaluated six classifiers on the held-out test set.\n",
    "The results revealed a clear configuration issue with the gradient boosting\n",
    "models double class-balancing arose from applying SMOTE to the training set\n",
    "while simultaneously passing class weight parameters to each model, suppressing\n",
    "Recall to unacceptable levels across XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Accuracy | Precision | Recall | F1-Score | ROC-AUC |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Logistic Regression | 72.42% | 30.39% | **75.88%** | 43.40% | 81.33% |\n",
    "| Decision Tree | 75.32% | 31.61% | 66.28% | 42.80% | 79.50% |\n",
    "| Random Forest | 77.47% | 33.97% | 65.38% | 44.71% | 81.32% |\n",
    "| XGBoost | 85.78% | 48.06% | 25.33% | 33.18% | 81.36% |\n",
    "| LightGBM | 86.11% | 50.39% | 20.77% | 29.41% | 81.55% |\n",
    "| CatBoost | 86.44% | 54.19% | 17.35% | 26.28% | **82.00%** |\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic Regression leads on Recall (**75.88%**) while CatBoost leads on\n",
    "ROC-AUC (**82.00%**). Before final model selection, two corrective actions\n",
    "are applied in Section 6.8:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Gradient boosting models are retrained without class weight parameters,\n",
    "   since SMOTE has already addressed the training set imbalance.\n",
    "2. Decision threshold tuning is applied to the best ROC-AUC model to\n",
    "   optimise the Recall/Precision trade-off."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6859a49f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6.8 Hyperparameter Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial training round identified two issues requiring correction before\n",
    "final model selection:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Double class-balancing** — gradient boosting models were trained with\n",
    "   both SMOTE-resampled data and class weight parameters simultaneously,\n",
    "   causing over-correction toward the majority class and critically low\n",
    "   Recall values.\n",
    "2. **Default decision threshold** — all models used the default 0.5\n",
    "   classification threshold, which may not be optimal for maximising Recall\n",
    "   on an imbalanced dataset in a clinical context.\n",
    "\n",
    "This section addresses both issues through two targeted interventions:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **6.8.1** — Gradient boosting models are retrained without class weight\n",
    "  parameters, isolating the effect of SMOTE alone.\n",
    "- **6.8.2** — Decision threshold tuning is applied to identify the optimal\n",
    "  threshold for maximising Recall while maintaining acceptable Precision.\n",
    "- **6.8.3** — All tuned models are compared against the initial results to\n",
    "  assess improvement."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "abd42aef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6.8.1 Retraining Models Without Class Weights\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial training round applied `class_weight=\"balanced\"` to Logistic\n",
    "Regression and Random Forest, and equivalent class weight parameters to\n",
    "the three gradient boosting models, alongside SMOTE-resampled training\n",
    "data. This section retrains all five models without class weight parameters\n",
    "to isolate the effect of SMOTE alone and assess whether the combined\n",
    "class-balancing strategy was responsible for the suboptimal Recall values\n",
    "observed in the gradient boosting models."
   ]
  },
