    "**Observation — Final Comparison Including HPT Models**\n",
    "\n",
    "The complete model comparison confirms a clear and consistent finding:\n",
    "all tuned models converge to a narrow Recall band of **75.00%–75.88%**\n",
    "after threshold optimisation, regardless of whether hyperparameter\n",
    "tuning was applied. This confirms that **decision threshold optimisation\n",
    "is the dominant factor** in achieving the target Recall level on this\n",
    "dataset not the choice of algorithm or hyperparameter configuration.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Logistic Regression remains the Recall leader at 75.88%** without\n",
    "any threshold adjustment, retraining, or hyperparameter search.\n",
    "Hyperparameter tuning of XGBoost and CatBoost produced strong\n",
    "cross-validated Recall estimates (83.40% and 84.55% respectively) but\n",
    "failed to generalise to the test set, with both models achieving only\n",
    "61–64% Recall before threshold correction. This overfitting to the\n",
    "SMOTE-resampled training distribution is an important finding that\n",
    "warrants acknowledgement in the limitations section.\n",
    "\n",
    "The HPT models offer no meaningful advantage over their threshold-tuned\n",
    "counterparts in terms of test set performance, and their lower ROC-AUC\n",
    "scores (81.10%–81.13% vs 81.33%–82.00%) make them weaker candidates\n",
    "for final selection."
   ]
