   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 7. Explainability — SHAP and LIME\n",
    "\n",
    "Predictive accuracy alone is insufficient for a clinical decision-support\n",
    "tool. Healthcare professionals require explanations before acting on\n",
    "algorithmic recommendations they need to understand not just *what* the\n",
    "model predicts, but *why* it made that prediction for a specific patient.\n",
    "\n",
    "This section implements two complementary Explainable AI (XAI) techniques\n",
    "to interpret the predictions of the final CatBoost model:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SHAP** (SHapley Additive exPlanations) provides theoretically\n",
    "  grounded feature attributions based on cooperative game theory. SHAP\n",
    "  values quantify the contribution of each feature to a prediction,\n",
    "  both globally across the entire dataset and locally for individual\n",
    "  patients.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **LIME** (Local Interpretable Model-Agnostic Explanations) generates\n",
    "  locally faithful explanations for individual predictions by fitting a\n",
    "  simple linear surrogate model around a single observation. LIME produces\n",
    "  human-readable condition statements that are accessible to non-technical\n",
    "  stakeholders.\n",
    "\n",
    "Together, SHAP and LIME transform the CatBoost model from a black box\n",
    "into a transparent decision-support tool enabling clinicians to\n",
    "understand, verify, and trust the predictions it produces.\n",
    "\n",
    "The explainability analysis is organised as follows:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **7.1** — SHAP Global Feature Importance\n",
    "- **7.2** — SHAP Summary Plot\n",
    "- **7.3** — SHAP Waterfall Plot (individual patient)\n",
    "- **7.4** — SHAP Dependence Plots\n",
    "- **7.5** — LIME Local Explanation\n",
    "- **7.6** — Explainability Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f1cdb89c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7.1 SHAP Global Feature Importance\n",
    "\n",
    "Global SHAP analysis computes the mean absolute SHAP value for each feature\n",
    "across all test set predictions. This provides a population-level view of\n",
    "which features the model relies on most when making predictions the global\n",
    "feature importance ranking.\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike tree-based feature importance scores, which measure how often a\n",
    "feature is used in splits, SHAP values measure the actual contribution of\n",
    "each feature to each prediction. This makes SHAP importance more reliable\n",
    "and directly interpretable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 101,
   "id": "6acf36ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "✅ SHAP explainer initialised\n",
      "   SHAP values shape : (85818, 14)\n",
      "   Test set shape    : (85818, 14)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import shap\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialise SHAP TreeExplainer for CatBoost\n",
    "explainer   = shap.TreeExplainer(final_model)\n",
    "shap_values = explainer.shap_values(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ SHAP explainer initialised\")\n",
    "print(f\"   SHAP values shape : {shap_values.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Test set shape    : {X_test_scaled.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
