    "## 7.5 LIME Local Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "LIME generates a local explanation for a single prediction by fitting a\n",
    "simple linear model in the neighbourhood of that observation. Unlike SHAP,\n",
    "which provides exact feature attributions, LIME produces human-readable\n",
    "condition statements for example, **\"BMI > 30 increases risk\"** that\n",
    "are accessible to non-technical stakeholders such as patients and\n",
    "non-specialist clinicians.\n",
    "\n",
    "LIME is applied to the same high-risk patient examined in the SHAP\n",
    "waterfall plot, allowing direct comparison of the two explanation methods\n",
    "for the same prediction."
   ]
