   "source": [
    "## 8.1 Project Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This project developed an end-to-end machine learning system for predicting\n",
    "Type 2 diabetes risk using the CDC Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System\n",
    "(BRFSS) 2023 survey data. The system combines predictive accuracy with\n",
    "Explainable AI techniques SHAP and LIME to produce transparent,\n",
    "clinician-friendly predictions that support early screening and preventive\n",
    "healthcare decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The project addressed all six specific objectives defined in Section 1:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Objective | Outcome |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Collect and preprocess healthcare data | BRFSS 2023 dataset loaded, recoded, and cleaned 429,086 records retained across 14 features |\n",
    "| Perform exploratory data analysis | Comprehensive univariate, bivariate, and multivariate analysis conducted across all features and demographic subgroups |\n",
    "| Build and evaluate ML models | Six classifiers trained and evaluated on a held-out test set using five performance metrics |\n",
    "| Compare classification algorithms | Full comparison table produced gradient boosting models identified as strongest after threshold tuning |\n",
    "| Implement SHAP and LIME | Global and local SHAP explanations generated; LIME local explanations produced for individual patients |\n",
    "| Develop an interactive dashboard | FastAPI backend and Next.js frontend developed for real-time single and batch prediction with explainability |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "34e2e8ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8.2 Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data and Preprocessing**\n",
    "\n",
    "The BRFSS 2023 dataset required substantial preprocessing before modelling.\n",
    "BRFSS-specific coded responses representing *Don't Know*, *Refused*, and\n",
    "*Not Applicable* were identified and recoded across nine variables. The\n",
    "`PHYSHLTH` variable required special handling, with the code `88` (zero bad\n",
    "days) recoded to `0` before general missing-value treatment to avoid\n",
    "discarding 256,565 valid responses. BMI was stored as an integer multiplied\n",
    "by 100 and required rescaling. Following target variable construction\n",
    "excluding gestational diabetes and uncertain responses the final analytical\n",
    "dataset contained **429,086 records** with a **6.2:1 class imbalance**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Exploratory Data Analysis**\n",
    "\n",
    "EDA confirmed that several features show clear separation between diabetic\n",
    "and non-diabetic respondents. Diabetes prevalence increases progressively\n",
    "with age, peaking in respondents aged 65 and above. A strong socioeconomic\n",
    "gradient was identified prevalence is highest among the lowest income\n",
    "groups and declines consistently as income rises. General health, hypertension,\n",
    "kidney disease, and heart disease showed the strongest bivariate associations\n",
    "with the target variable. Native American and Black respondents exhibited\n",
    "the highest diabetes prevalence across racial groups.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Modelling**\n",
    "\n",
    "Six classifiers were trained and evaluated. The initial training round\n",
    "revealed that gradient boosting models XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost\n",
    "produced critically low Recall values (17–25%) at the default 0.5 decision\n",
    "threshold, despite achieving the highest ROC-AUC scores (81–82%). Logistic\n",
    "Regression achieved the highest initial Recall at **75.88%**. Decision\n",
    "threshold tuning successfully recovered Recall from all gradient boosting\n",
    "models to approximately 75%, confirming that the models had strong ranking\n",
    "ability but required threshold adjustment to operate at the correct\n",
    "sensitivity level.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Final Model**\n",
    "\n",
    "**CatBoost with threshold tuning** was selected as the final model based on\n",
    "the highest ROC-AUC (**82.00%**) and F1-Score (**44.26%**) among models\n",
    "meeting the minimum Recall threshold of 75%. The model correctly identifies\n",
    "approximately three in every four diabetic patients in the test population.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Explainability**\n",
    "\n",
    "SHAP global analysis identified the most influential features at the\n",
    "population level. SHAP waterfall plots provided patient-level explanations\n",
    "showing exactly how each feature contributed to an individual prediction.\n",
    "LIME generated human-readable condition statements for the same predictions,\n",
    "providing a complementary explanation accessible to non-technical\n",
    "stakeholders. The agreement between SHAP and LIME for individual predictions\n",
    "increases confidence in the reliability of the explanations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cd8de7f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8.3 Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset limitations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The BRFSS dataset is based on **self-reported survey responses**, introducing\n",
    "  potential recall bias and social desirability bias. Respondents may\n",
    "  under-report behaviors such as smoking or over-report physical activity.\n",
    "- The diabetes diagnosis in the target variable (`DIABETE4`) is\n",
    "  **self-reported** rather than laboratory-confirmed, meaning some positive\n",
    "  cases may be misclassified.\n",
    "- The BRFSS survey population **over-represents certain demographics** \n",
    "  particularly older, white, and more educated respondents which may limit\n",
    "  the model's generalisability to underrepresented groups.\n",
    "- The dataset is a **cross-sectional survey**, capturing a single point in\n",
    "  time. Longitudinal data would provide stronger evidence of causal\n",
    "  relationships between risk factors and diabetes onset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Modelling limitations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SMOTE** was applied to the full training set rather than within each\n",
    "  cross-validation fold, which may introduce a small degree of data leakage\n",
    "  into the cross-validation process.\n",
    "- **Hyperparameter tuning** was limited to decision threshold optimisation\n",
    "  due to computational constraints. A full GridSearchCV or Optuna-based\n",
    "  hyperparameter search may yield further performance improvements.\n",
    "- The **6.2:1 class imbalance** in the test set means that even with high\n",
    "  Recall, the model produces a large number of false positives a Precision\n",
    "  of approximately 31% means roughly two in every three flagged patients\n",
    "  are not diabetic.\n",
    "- The model was trained and evaluated on **US survey data** and may not\n",
    "  generalise to populations in other countries or healthcare systems,\n",
    "  including Kenya and East Africa where this project was developed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Explainability limitations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- LIME explanations are **locally faithful but globally inconsistent**\n",
    "  they approximate the model's behaviour in a small neighbourhood around\n",
    "  each prediction and may not reflect the model's global decision logic.\n",
    "- SHAP values for this dataset are derived from **scaled feature values**,\n",
    "  requiring careful mapping back to original units for clinical\n",
    "  interpretation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "09fff260",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8.4 Recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "**For clinical deployment**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The model should be used as a **screening support tool only** not as\n",
    "  a replacement for clinical laboratory testing or professional medical\n",
    "  assessment. Patients flagged as high risk should be referred for\n",
    "  follow-up fasting blood glucose or HbA1c testing.\n",
    "- A **minimum Recall threshold of 75%** should be maintained in any\n",
    "  deployed version. If the model is retrained on new data, threshold\n",
    "  tuning should be repeated to maintain this sensitivity level.\n",
    "- **SHAP explanations** should be presented alongside every prediction\n",
    "  to ensure clinicians can interrogate and verify the model's reasoning\n",
    "  before acting on its output.\n",
    "\n",
    "**For future model development**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Hyperparameter tuning** via GridSearchCV or Optuna should be applied\n",
    "  to XGBoost and CatBoost to determine whether further performance gains\n",
    "  are achievable beyond threshold optimisation.\n",
    "- **SMOTE within cross-validation folds** should replace the current\n",
    "  approach to eliminate the residual data leakage risk.\n",
    "- The model should be **retrained periodically** as new BRFSS survey\n",
    "  data becomes available to prevent model drift and maintain calibration.\n",
    "- **Laboratory-confirmed diabetes diagnoses** from a clinical dataset\n",
    "  would strengthen the target variable and improve model reliability.\n",
    "- Extending the feature set to include **HbA1c levels**, **fasting glucose**,\n",
    "  and **family history of diabetes** if available would likely improve\n",
    "  predictive performance significantly.\n",
    "\n",
    "**For the platform**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **User authentication and prediction history** should be added to enable\n",
    "  longitudinal tracking of individual risk assessments over time.\n",
    "- **Mobile accessibility** would extend the platform's reach to community\n",
    "  health workers and primary care settings in low-resource environments.\n",
    "- **Integration with electronic health records (EHR)** would enable\n",
    "  automated risk flagging at the population level without requiring manual\n",
    "  data entry."
   ]
  },
